[{:adr/consequences "{:test_vector_integrity \"every hex literal in test/sha256d/core_test.cljc and the midstate fixture is copy-pasted from a freshly-run `python3 -c \\\"...hashlib...\\\"` / `shasum -a 256` invocation in this session's transcript, with explicit len()==64 assertions before use, not retyped from memory -- prompted by a live transcription near-miss (a hand-typed copy of the well-known million-'a' vector was one character short) during authoring\", :portability_bug_found_and_fixed \"sha256d.core/pad's length-field encoding originally shifted by up to 56 bits, valid on a JVM long (unsigned-bit-shift-right is 64-bit-aware there) but silently wrong under cljs (JS bitwise ops mask shift counts to 5 bits); the cljs_verify.cljs run under node caught it (2 of 4 known-answer checks + the midstate property check failed) where the JVM suite alone did not, since it never exercised the cljs code path. Fixed via sha256d.core/u64be-bytes (quot/mod split into 32-bit halves, no shift past bit 31); all 14 JVM tests / 5144 assertions and all 5 cljs checks pass after the fix.\", :honest_first_run_findings \"docs/evolution-log.md's initial entry records 3 clojure -M:evolve runs: no stable champion (2/3 runs land in a single 1%-proximity cluster), and evolve-round's recombination-only-among-elite-values causes generation-over-generation gene diversity loss -- both logged as real findings/follow-ups, not smoothed into a false 'discovery' narrative\", :non_duplication_of_adr_2607012230 \"cross-referenced the concurrently-landed kotoba-lang Bitcoin mining/wallet substrate ADR; the two are complementary (host-injected production crypto there vs from-scratch searchable/benchmarkable algorithm-level code here), not overlapping, and sha256d.core is noted as a candidate future host-crypto-free backend option for kotoba-lang/crypto (not attempted in this ADR)\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["sha256d-clj lives at orgs/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj (github.com/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj, private), not under kotoba-lang -- cross-cutting -clj foundation lib per manifest/repos.edn's org-routing rule, not a language-substrate lib" "the matrixflow.net/case-study/110 reference is about AlphaProof/Gemini Deep Think/AlphaEvolve/FunSearch, NOT SHA-256/Bitcoin -- the transferable idea is the evolutionary-search-over-a-scored-population shape, reframed here with correctness as a hard gate (not a fitness term) because a hash function cannot be 'approximately' correct" "sha256d.core's round-function primitives (Ch/Maj/Sigma0/Sigma1/rotr32/add32) are shared .cljc with NO #?(:clj :cljs) split -- every op is bit-position-local or a bounded-width add, sign-representation-invariant on both platforms; the one place that genuinely needs a platform split is nothing in this repo post-fix, since the u64be-bytes fix made even the length-field encoding fully portable via quot/mod instead of wide shifts" "this repo is NOT a duplicate of ADR-2607012230's kotoba-lang/btc-crypto+btc-mining: that stack's SHA-256 is host-injected (kotoba-lang/crypto contract, vetted platform crypto for production use); sha256d-clj is deliberately from-scratch and host-crypto-free specifically so its formula/implementation-strategy space is searchable/benchmarkable, which a host crypto API black box structurally cannot be" "every test-vector hex literal in this repo was generated via Python hashlib / the system shasum utility and cross-checked by exact string length, never hand-transcribed from memory -- a live near-miss during authoring (a by-hand copy of the well-known million-'a' NIST vector came out one hex character short) is the concrete reason for this rule" "the cljs portability proof (test/sha256d/cljs_verify.cljs, run via `clojure -M:cljs && node target/cljs-verify.js`) caught a real bug the JVM test suite alone did not: JS bitwise shift operators mask the shift count to 5 bits (x >>> 40 behaves as x >>> 8), which broke the original pad function's 64-bit big-endian length-field encoding (fixed in sha256d.core/u64be-bytes by splitting into two 32-bit halves via quot/mod)" "docs/evolution-log.md's first entry is an honest negative result from an actual run, not a fabricated discovery: no stable champion across 3 runs (2 of 3 land in one proximity cluster -- Ranking found no significant difference at the current gene-pool size/noise floor), and evolve-round loses gene diversity generation-over-generation because recombination only reintroduces variants already present among elites" "ADDENDUM 2026-07-02: the tournament ran 17 rounds (see docs/evolution-log.md summary table). The ONLY lever that moved single-hash throughput was removing per-operation runtime overhead: compress-primitive-inline (JVM, unboxed round loop + inlined ch/maj) ~2.7x, compress-v8-inline (cljs, Int32Array) ~3.6x -- each a platform-only opt-in fast path, portable compress stays the default. Ch/Maj formula and schedule data structure NEVER mattered (measured, incl. a zero-alloc long-array schedule that only ties precompute); software 2-way multi-buffer is ~6% SLOWER (register spills). Allocation never mattered single-thread or parallel." "ADDENDUM 2026-07-02: the parallel nonce-search plateau (~4.6x on 10 cores) is all-core turbo FREQUENCY scaling, NOT GC/allocation -- proven by a GC-MXBean diagnostic (<1% pause) + an all-cores-hot test (single-thread drops to 46% = the per-thread parallel rate; 46% x 10 = 4.6). No code change lifts it; search-nonce-parallel scales as well as the hardware allows." "ADDENDUM 2026-07-02: mining composes midstate + fast compress via header-hash-with/search-nonce/search-nonce-parallel = ~4.4x per-nonce over naive full-header hashing (1.59x midstate x 2.78x fast compress), ~272k nonce/s on 10 cores, all bit-identical. Validated against the REAL Bitcoin genesis block (block 0, hash 000000000019d668...) on JVM+V8; search-nonce recovers Satoshi's genesis nonce 2083236893. Fixtures independently verified via Python hashlib." "ADDENDUM 2026-07-02 (cryptanalysis / inverse direction, sha256d.mitm + docs/preimage-mitm-cosci.md): below-brute-force PREIMAGE algorithms are real (MITM/splice-and-cut/biclique) and the co-scientist search DESIGNS them over the message-schedule dependency graph. run-mitm RUNS one on the real 32-bit round function: 8-round SHA-256 partial preimage in 2049 chunk-evals vs 2,325,617 brute = measured/verified ~1135x. Word-granularity dies at ~24 rounds; bit-level neutral bits give NO sound gain over word-level (tested: a bit of W_i is neutral for a chunk iff the whole word is unused). The ~45-round/2^255.5 record needs bicliques (differential trails) -- described, NOT fabricated." "ADDENDUM 2026-07-02: FULL 64-round SHA-256 is NOT broken and this repo does NOT fabricate a break. Honest reasoning recorded: a below-2^256 full-round preimage is conjectured not to exist; a co-scientist / AlphaEvolve / AlphaProof-Nexus-style search cannot conjure one (it searches within known-technique templates and a proof of a false statement cannot be found), and one-wayness is a circuit lower bound beyond known mathematics no prover can establish. Defensive risk: full-round break is a negligible tail (best 2^255.5 on 45/64 rounds; Grover only 2^128, sequential/infeasible); real risks are implementation/misuse (length-extension->HMAC, low-entropy->KDF, non-constant-time); AI-assisted cryptanalysis is a monitoring signal that may accelerate reduced-round records but not the full-round tail."], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "sha256d-clj", :adr/related ["CLAUDE.md" "manifest/repos.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607012230-kotoba-lang-btc-mining-wallet-substrate.md" "orgs/kotoba-lang/eth-crypto/src/eth_crypto/core.cljc" "orgs/kotoba-lang/num/test/num/cljs_verify.cljs" "orgs/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj/README.md" "orgs/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj/docs/evolution-log.md" "orgs/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj/docs/preimage-mitm-cosci.md" "orgs/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj/src/sha256d/mitm.cljc"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607012300-sha256d-clj-portable-cosci-tournament", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-02", :adr/decision "{:new_repo {:path \"orgs/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj\", :remote \"com-junkawasaki\", :visibility :private, :method \"clojure -M:test green (14 tests, 5144 assertions) + clojure -M:cljs && node target/cljs-verify.js green (5 checks) BEFORE git init/commit; git init, one commit, gh repo create com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj --private --source=. --remote=origin --push\", :head_sha \"847da432443ad401dd1d028578a980c4265bb05b\", :modules {:core \"FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 + sha256d (double SHA-256) over plain byte-value sequences; ch-fn/maj-fn injection seam via 2/4-arity compress and sha256-bytes/sha256d-bytes overloads\", :ops \"gene pool: ch-alt (z ^ (x & (y^z))), maj-alt ((x&y) | (z&(x|y))) -- both algebraically proven equivalent in doc-comments and exhaustively re-checked in test\", :midstate \"Bitcoin header mining midstate caching: cache compression state after the header's constant first 64-byte chunk, skip re-compressing it per nonce attempt\", :evolve \"Generation/Reflection/Ranking/Evolution/Proximity/Meta-review tournament under run-tournament; reflect is a hard correctness gate, rank does pairwise Elo benchmarking with a 1%-is-a-draw threshold\"}}, :manifest_registration {:repos_edn \"added \\\"orgs/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj\\\" to :extra-projects (local edit + commit; superproject was confirmed in sync with origin/main via git fetch + gh api compare + git merge --ff-only immediately beforehand, so no API-single-entry-commit workaround was needed for this file)\", :west_yml \"added one project entry (name/remote/revision/path/groups) by hand at the correct alphabetical position, NOT via a full nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs regen -- --check was already STALE before this change (pre-existing unrelated child-repo pin drift from concurrent activity); verified byte-for-byte identical to the generator's own output for this path by running a full regen to a scratch copy, diffing, and reverting before committing\", :verify \"pin (847da43...) == orgs/com-junkawasaki/sha256d-clj@main HEAD confirmed; `west update sha256d-clj` resolves and checks out the pinned revision cleanly (left a normal detached-HEAD-then-checkout-main note, not an error)\", :deliberately_not_done \"nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs was run to completion once to produce a scratch diff for verification, then its output was discarded (restored the hand-edited version) rather than committed, to avoid bundling ~dozens of unrelated pre-existing pin advances into this one-entry registration -- same pin-regression-trap avoidance as ADR-2607011816\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user request 2026-07-01 (JP): 'bitcoin の sha256 を https://www.matrixflow.net/case-study/110/ などを参考に効率的に、導出する repo を cljc で設計してみて, google cosientist の アプローチで' -- design a cljc repo that efficiently derives Bitcoin's SHA-256, referencing the matrixflow case study, using a 'Google co-scientist' approach\", :investigated [\"WebFetch on matrixflow.net/case-study/110 showed it covers AlphaProof/Gemini Deep Think/AlphaEvolve/FunSearch, not SHA-256 or Bitcoin at all -- corrected the premise to the user before designing\" \"WebSearch confirmed Google co-scientist's 6-agent architecture (Generation/Reflection/Ranking/Evolution/Proximity/Meta-review under a Supervisor, Elo-based tournament-of-ideas) and AlphaEvolve's evolutionary-program-database + LLM-mutation search shape (48-multiplication 4x4 matrix mult, beating Strassen's 56-year bound)\" \"grep across manifest/repos.edn org-routing comment confirmed 'cross-cutting 基盤 -clj -> com-junkawasaki' placement rule; grepped orgs/kotoba-lang/eth-crypto/src/eth_crypto/core.cljc and confirmed no existing from-scratch public SHA-256 to avoid duplicating (only a private hmac-sha256 helper for ECDSA nonce derivation)\" \"inspected orgs/kotoba-lang/num and orgs/kotoba-lang/eth-crypto as templates for deps.edn/README/CI-workflow/cljs-verify-pattern conventions\" \"AskUserQuestion with the owner resolved two open design forks before writing code: (1) self-contained deterministic search vs a real Workflow-orchestrated multi-agent loop -- chose self-contained/deterministic; (2) design-doc-only vs full scaffold+push now -- chose full pipeline now, per CLAUDE.md's standing new-project authorization\" \"mid-session, git fetch on the superproject showed '(forced update)' + 'refusing to merge unrelated histories' on origin/main -- gh api compare confirmed the documented shallow-clone false-positive pattern (status: ahead, behind_by: 0, merge_base_commit == old local tip), resolved via git fetch --deepen=20 rather than treated as a real force-push; the fast-forward pulled in a concurrent, unrelated ADR-2607012230 (kotoba-lang Bitcoin mining/wallet substrate) which was then cross-referenced for a non-duplication argument\"], :risk \"a hash function has no partial credit -- an evolutionary/co-scientist-style search that treats correctness as a soft fitness term (as AlphaEvolve does for matrix multiplication, where a slightly-wrong answer is just a lower score) would produce something that looks like it's exploring implementations while silently accepting incorrect ones; mitigated by making sha256d.evolve/reflect a hard disqualifying gate, run before any benchmarking, never contributing to the Elo score\"}", :adr/followups ["grow sha256d.ops's gene pool (loop-unrolling degree, message-schedule buffer reuse, batch/lane-parallel hashing) -- today's 2x2 search space is small enough that Ranking's findings are dominated by benchmark noise per the evolution-log's first entry" "run sha256d.evolve/run-tournament under node, not just the JVM -- the cljs portability proof covers core/ops/midstate correctness only, not the tournament itself" "evaluate offering sha256d.core as an alternative host-crypto-free backend for kotoba-lang/crypto's SHA-256 data contract -- not attempted in this ADR"], :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"a real Workflow-orchestrated multi-agent loop (literal Generation/Reflection/Ranking/Evolution/Proximity/Meta-review subagents proposing and verifying code diffs each run)\", :rejected_because \"owner's explicit choice via AskUserQuestion: costs tokens per run and needs Workflow opt-in, versus a self-contained deterministic harness that ships in the repo and needs no LLM to operate at run time; left as a documented possible follow-up\"} {:option \"score correctness as a fitness term instead of a hard gate, closer to how AlphaEvolve scores an imperfect matrix-multiplication algorithm\", :rejected_because \"SHA-256 has no notion of partial credit -- would just be a more confusing way to implement the same disqualify-on-mismatch behavior sha256d.evolve/reflect already does directly\"} {:option \"hand-derive the real Bitcoin genesis block header as the midstate test fixture, for a more famous/recognizable example\", :rejected_because \"same transcription-risk class as the million-'a' near-miss, for a 160-hex-character value with no independent local oracle to check it against at authoring time; used a clearly-labeled synthetic header cross-checked via Python hashlib instead\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607012300: sha256d-clj -- portable .cljc SHA-256/SHA-256d + a Google-co-scientist/AlphaEvolve-shaped evolutionary benchmark tournament"}]